            <ArticleTitle>Perforation of a saphenous vein graft during percutaneous angioplasty: demonstration by means of intravascular ultrasound and consequent treatment with a polytetrafluoroethylene-covered stent.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e15-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ijcard.2007.12.053</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of a perforation of the saphenous vein graft during percutaneous angioplasty and its subsequent implantation with a polytetrafluoroethylene-covered stent. Angiographic as well as intravascular images of the site of perforation are provided.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
